Feature: The battlefield
  The battlefield is the big picture in the middle of the app. It shows the valley in 3D, as
  your camera sees it from above: the forest, the lanes, the lake and the mountains. The app
  draws the towers, your drones, the enemy drones that your team sees and the [[fog]] on the
  picture.

  The picture comes from the 3D view of the game. It has no drones in it, so it does not show
  what the fog hides. Each drone on the battlefield stands on a line from its shadow on the
  ground, so you can see how high it flies. Without the 3D view, the app draws the plain map of
  the valley in the same perspective.

  At the start, the camera looks at the base of your team, towards the enemy. W, A, S and D, or
  the arrow keys, move the camera. If you put the mouse at an edge of the battlefield, the camera
  moves that way. Q and E turn the camera 45° to the left and to the right. The mouse wheel moves
  the camera nearer to the ground, or further from it.

  The minimap is at the left of the bottom bar. It shows the whole field and the area that the
  camera sees. Click the minimap, and the camera looks at that point. Space moves the camera to
  the selected drones.

  Expectation: The battlefield shows the valley in 3D
    The 3D view loads the valley first. That takes some minutes after a game starts, and the app
    shows the plain map until then.

    When the commander waits for the battlefield
    Then the battlefield picture in the app is live

  Expectation: The camera starts at the base of the team
    When the commander joins the game
    Then the point of the battlefield camera is the Blue base
    And the heading of the battlefield camera is 0 deg

  Expectation: A click on the minimap moves the camera there
    When the commander clicks the west tower on the minimap
    Then the point of the battlefield camera is the west tower

  Expectation: The keys move the camera across the field
    Given the point of the battlefield camera is the Blue base
    When the commander pans the battlefield to the front
    Then the distance from the Blue base to the battlefield camera's point is at least 100 m

  Expectation: The mouse at the edge of the battlefield moves the camera
    Given the point of the battlefield camera is the Blue base
    When the commander moves the mouse to the top edge of the battlefield
    Then the distance from the Blue base to the battlefield camera's point is at least 100 m

  Expectation: E turns the camera to the right
    Given the heading of the battlefield camera is 0 deg
    When the commander turns the battlefield camera to the right
    Then the heading of the battlefield camera is 45 deg

  Expectation: The mouse wheel moves the camera nearer to the ground
    Given the height of the battlefield camera is 600 m
    When the commander zooms the battlefield in
    Then the height of the battlefield camera is at most 500 m

  Expectation: Space moves the camera to the selected drone
    Given the first Blue drone is in the west circle
    And the selected drone is the first Blue drone
    When the commander centres the battlefield on the selected drone
    Then the point of the battlefield camera is the west tower
